---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { PARTS, labels } from '../../lib/kinetic/model';
import { levels } from '../../lib/kinetic/levels';
import '../../styles/kinetic.css';
---
<Layout title="Kinetic Workshop" description="Build a small machine. Follow a marble. Make a puzzle of your own.">
  <section class="kinetic wrap" id="kinetic">
    <header class="kinetic-heading"><div><a class="kinetic-back" href="/play/">← BACK TO THE ARCADE</a><h1>Kinetic <em>Workshop.</em></h1><p>A little gravity. A little ingenuity.</p></div><span class="kinetic-edition">MECHANICAL STUDIES<br/>BUILD / RELEASE / REFINE</span></header>
    <noscript>This workshop needs JavaScript and WebAssembly for its local physics engine.</noscript>
    <div class="kinetic-modes" role="group" aria-label="Workshop mode"><button data-mode="challenges" aria-pressed="true">Challenges</button><button data-mode="workshop" aria-pressed="false">Workshop</button><span id="kinetic-context">Six small problems. Many possible solutions.</span></div>
    <div class="kinetic-levels" id="kinetic-levels">{levels.map((level,i)=><button data-level={level.id} aria-pressed={i===0?'true':'false'}><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>{level.title}<i data-complete={level.id} aria-label="Not completed">○</i></button>)}</div>
    <div class="kinetic-example-bar" id="kinetic-examples" hidden><label>Start from <select id="kinetic-example"><option value="blank">Blank board</option><option value="0">A quiet descent</option><option value="1">Over the gap</option><option value="2">A clockwork funnel</option></select></label><button id="kinetic-new">New machine</button><button id="kinetic-test">Test as a challenge</button><button id="kinetic-author" hidden>Return to authoring</button></div>
    <div class="kinetic-status" id="kinetic-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Loading the workshop…</div><button id="kinetic-retry" hidden>Retry physics loading</button>
    <div class="kinetic-workspace">
      <div class="kinetic-main">
        <div class="kinetic-transport"><button id="kinetic-run" class="kinetic-primary">Release ▶</button><button id="kinetic-step">Step +1</button><button id="kinetic-edit">Return to edit</button><button id="kinetic-restart">Restart run</button><label class="kinetic-pace">Pace <select id="kinetic-speed"><option value="1">1×</option><option value="0.25">¼×</option></select></label></div>
        <div class="kinetic-board" id="kinetic-board"><canvas id="kinetic-canvas" tabindex="0" aria-label="Mechanical board. Select a part and click to place. Arrow keys move the selected part, R rotates, Delete removes, Space runs or pauses."></canvas><div class="kinetic-board-label"><span id="kinetic-phase">EDIT / LAYOUT</span><span id="kinetic-clock">0.00 s / 30 s</span></div></div>
        <div class="kinetic-view-tools"><button id="kinetic-zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in">＋</button><button id="kinetic-zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out">−</button><button id="kinetic-view-reset">Reset view</button><button id="kinetic-view-toggle">Use 2D view</button><span>Wheel to zoom · right-drag / two fingers to pan</span></div>
        <div class="kinetic-palette" role="group" aria-label="Placement tools"><button data-tool="select" aria-pressed="true">↖ Select</button><button data-tool="pan" aria-pressed="false">✥ Pan</button>{PARTS.map(kind=><button data-tool={kind} aria-pressed="false">{labels[kind]} <span data-remaining={kind}></span></button>)}</div>
        <div class="kinetic-edit-actions"><button id="kinetic-undo">Undo</button><button id="kinetic-redo">Redo</button><button id="kinetic-copy">Duplicate</button><button id="kinetic-delete">Delete</button><label><input id="kinetic-snap" type="checkbox" checked/> Snap to grid / 15°</label></div>
        <section class="kinetic-replay"><div class="kinetic-section-title"><h2>Follow the journey</h2><span id="kinetic-score">0 / 1 collected</span></div><div class="kinetic-replay-actions"><button id="kinetic-replay">Review last run</button><button id="kinetic-replay-play" disabled>Play replay</button><input type="range" id="kinetic-timeline" min="0" max="0" value="0" aria-label="Replay position" disabled/><output id="kinetic-replay-time">0.00 s</output></div><p class="kinetic-hint">Replay is read-only. Return to edit restores the launch layout, not an intermediate physics state.</p><div class="kinetic-events" id="kinetic-events"></div></section>
      </div>
      <aside class="kinetic-controls">
        <section><div class="kinetic-section-title"><h2 id="kinetic-title">First Descent</h2><span id="kinetic-badge">CHALLENGE</span></div><p id="kinetic-description" class="kinetic-hint"></p><details id="kinetic-hint-panel"><summary>A small hint</summary><p id="kinetic-hint" class="kinetic-hint"></p></details><p class="kinetic-hint">Collect every ball within 30 seconds. A ball must rest in the cup for ½ second. Balls launch two seconds apart.</p></section>
        <section><div class="kinetic-section-title"><h2>Selected part</h2><span id="kinetic-selected">NONE</span></div><p id="kinetic-selection-help" class="kinetic-hint">Select a part, source or cup on the board. Choose a palette tool, then click the board to place a part.</p><div id="kinetic-properties" hidden><div class="kinetic-pair"><label>X <input id="kinetic-x" type="number" min="0.2" max="15.8" step="0.05"/></label><label>Y <input id="kinetic-y" type="number" min="0.2" max="9.8" step="0.05"/></label></div><label id="kinetic-angle-field">Angle (degrees) <input id="kinetic-angle" type="number" min="-180" max="180" step="1"/></label><label id="kinetic-length-field">Length <input id="kinetic-length" type="number" min="1" max="5" step="0.1"/></label><label id="kinetic-power-field">Launch speed / rotor speed <input id="kinetic-power" type="number" min="-3" max="12" step="0.1"/></label><label class="kinetic-checkbox" id="kinetic-locked-field"><input id="kinetic-locked" type="checkbox"/> Fixed in your challenge</label><button id="kinetic-rotate-left">Rotate −15°</button><button id="kinetic-rotate-right">Rotate +15°</button></div></section>
        <section id="kinetic-author-settings" hidden><div class="kinetic-section-title"><h2>Your puzzle</h2><span>AUTHOR</span></div><label>Name <input id="kinetic-name" maxlength="80" value="Untitled machine"/></label><label>Balls to collect <input id="kinetic-balls" type="number" min="1" max="5" step="1" value="1"/></label><p class="kinetic-hint">Move the source and cup on the board. Fixed parts stay in the exported puzzle; all other parts are your provisional solution.</p><h3 class="kinetic-small-heading">Player inventory</h3><div class="kinetic-budget">{PARTS.map(kind=><label>{labels[kind]}<input data-budget={kind} type="number" min="0" max="80" step="1" value="0"/></label>)}</div><p id="kinetic-proof" class="kinetic-hint">Not verified. Test and complete your puzzle before exporting a challenge.</p></section>
        <section><div class="kinetic-section-title"><h2>Keep the machine</h2><span>LOCAL</span></div><div class="kinetic-save-actions"><button id="kinetic-save">Save new copy</button><button id="kinetic-export">Export draft</button><button id="kinetic-export-challenge">Export challenge</button><button id="kinetic-import">Import machine</button><button id="kinetic-workshop-copy">Copy to Workshop</button></div><input type="file" id="kinetic-file" accept=".json,.kinetic.json" hidden/><p class="kinetic-hint">No accounts or uploads. Saves contain the design, not engine internals or the transient replay.</p></section>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <section class="kinetic-library"><div class="eyebrow">YOUR INVENTIONS</div><h2>A shelf of small machines<span>.</span></h2><p class="kinetic-hint">Open a saved draft to keep building. Import a challenge to solve someone else’s puzzle.</p><div id="kinetic-saves" class="kinetic-saves"></div></section>
    <details class="kinetic-notes"><summary>Controls, physics & limits</summary><p>Drag parts to move them. R rotates; Shift+R rotates back. Arrow keys nudge; Delete removes; Ctrl/Cmd+Z undoes, Shift+Ctrl/Cmd+Z redoes. Space releases or pauses when the canvas is focused. Use palette buttons and numeric properties for touch or keyboard placement.</p><p>Fixed 120 Hz Rapier 2D physics, with continuous collision detection on marbles. Launch pads are contact-triggered game impulses, not calibrated springs. A seesaw uses a real revolute joint; a rotating arm is motor-driven. Slow devices take longer without skipping physics steps. Rendering and replay do not change the simulation.</p><p>Limits: 80 parts, 5 marbles, 30 simulated seconds per run, 50 editing undo steps, 256 KB machine files. Hidden tabs pause and require manual resume. Local challenge verification is an authoring aid, not online anti-cheat or a guarantee that imported puzzles are solvable.</p></details>
  </section>
  <script>import '../../scripts/kinetic';</script>
</Layout>
